        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3e74ad65-b623-54be-aefa-1265c145e78f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Macworld, Soaps In Depth, MacLife, MacAddict\n- Companies: Apple Inc., Mac Publishing, Bauer Publications, International Data Group\n- People: David Bunnell, Andrew Fluegelman, Chris Breen\n- Places: San Francisco, California\n- Topics: magazine publishing, Apple products and software, soap opera magazines\n\nFacts:\n- Macworld started as a print magazine in 1984.\n- David Bunnell and Andrew Fluegelman founded Macworld, with Bunnell as publisher and Fluegelman as editor.\n- Macworld had the largest audited total and newsstand circulation among Macintosh-focused magazines in North America, at more than double the circulation of its nearest competitor, MacLife, formerly called MacAddict.\n- Soaps In Depth is a series of magazines created in 1997 by Bauer Publications for American soap opera viewers seeking more variety in soap-related magazine purchases.\n- Macworld is a website dedicated to Apple Inc. products and software.\n- Mac Publishing publishes Macworld and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.\n- International Data Group owns Mac Publishing as a division.\n- Chris Breen was a senior editor at Mac Publishing, which publishes the US edition of Macworld.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "079e7923-2570-50f3-b070-4687e69a7ffd",
        "text": "Page: Macworld. Sentence: Macworld is a web site dedicated to products and software of Apple Inc., published by Mac Publishing, which is headquartered in San Francisco, California.\nPage: Macworld. Sentence: It started life as a print magazine in 1984 and had the largest audited circulation (both total and newsstand) of Macintosh-focused magazines in North America, more than double its nearest competitor, \"MacLife\" (formerly \"MacAddict\").\nPage: Macworld. Sentence: \"Macworld\" was founded by David Bunnell (publisher) and Andrew Fluegelman (editor).\nPage: Soaps In Depth. Sentence: Soaps In Depth is a series of magazines created in 1997 by Bauer Publications to give American soap opera viewers more variety in their soap-related magazine purchases.\nPage: Chris Breen (editor). Sentence: He was a senior editor at Mac Publishing, a division of International Data Group which publishes the US edition of \"Macworld\".",
